blogs got stuck and the Germans were basically using him for target practice or sort of dropping shells getting closer and closer to him and he couldn't get out because he's stuck in all this mud. But there's worse things than mud. So Graves, remember I said he was dozing and he heard the people talking about lice. Lice are a big issue but there's also flies and fleas. So flies, Alexander Stewart again, he talks about filthy, fat, dirty flies, drawn by the dead bodies. Well, the flies must be, I mean, it must be all their Christmases come at once. Exactly, yeah.
格рей夫斯陷在泥里动弹不得，德国人基本上把他当成了活靶子，或者发射炮弹离他越来越近，而他因为深陷泥潭根本无法脱身。但比泥潭更糟糕的事还有很多。所以格里夫斯，还记得我刚才说他在打瞌睡时听到人们在谈论虱子吗？虱子是个大问题，但还有苍蝇和跳蚤。说到苍蝇，亚历山大·斯图尔特再次提到，尸体吸引了那些恶心、肥胖、肮脏的苍蝇。好吧，对苍蝇来说，这简直就像过圣诞节一样爽。完全是这样，没错。

61
00:28:08.000 --> 00:28:28.000
In the company headquarters dug out, he says, they were masked on the ceiling like a swarm of bees. And when a man was asleep, they would settle all around his mouth and over his face. So the corpses would be full of maggots, I guess. Exactly. Fleas. Everybody had fleas. You pretty much got fleas within weeks. They would get into underclothes.
他在连指挥部的防空洞里说，它们像一群蜜蜂一样密密麻麻地贴在天花板上。当一个人睡着时，它们会成群结队地落在他的嘴周围和脸上。所以我想，尸体一定爬满了蛆虫。确实如此。跳蚤。每个人都有跳蚤。你基本上在几周内就会染上跳蚤。它们会钻进内衣里。

62
00:28:28.000 --> 00:28:47.000
And what the soldiers would do is they would get candles. and they would kind of run the candle, the sort of lit candle along the seams of their underwear. And as one puts it, you could hear the eggs crackling as you kind of burned your own underpants with this candle. And then the lice,
